experiment: slotdrift
  the question      §56. §54's corruption was an INDEPENDENT COIN PER TRIAL and
                    §55 bounded short within-window runs at a quarter of the
                    deficit. The ARRANGEMENT of the errors across windows has
                    never been measured, and `retention` (a conflicting BLOCK
                    erases) beside §54 (interleaved conflicts average) says a
                    clamped store treats the two differently.
  the quantity      blocked = share of ERROR windows with an ERROR NEIGHBOUR in
                    the scored sequence. An error is a teaching window whose
                    modal slot differs from the session's modal assignment for
                    the object it showed -- §53's own `modal`, order kept.
  the null          EXACT, not a shuffle: 1 - (n-m)(n-m+1)/(n(n-1)) per creature
                    from its OWN n and m, so it carries no Monte-Carlo variance.
                    A 64-permutation shuffle checks the formula beside it.
  PRIMARY           blocked_obs - blocked_exact, meaned across creatures.
                    Signed: an anti-clustered index reads NEGATIVE.
  the boundaries    A: CI upper <  +0.0567 -- i.i.d., ARRANGEMENT REFUTED.
                    B: CI lower >  +0.0567 -- clustered, §54 UNDERSTATES.
                    C: anything else, or a half-width above 0.10.
                    Full scale up is +0.6965 at §53's rate; range is signed.
  session           900.0 s of simulated life x 60 sessions, 4 arms
  instrument        slotdrift   trial seed 0000000001357169   60 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  THE RATE AND THE ASSIGNMENT. `w_obs` must reproduce §53's 0.1712 on DERIVED --
  the same quantity from the same vectors by a different code path. `dark` is
  windows whose index never went live, dropped by `ctx_slot`'s own rule.
